1
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:28,960
Did you meet Liang?

2
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:31,920
But if you can't accept his offer,
you're stuck anyway.

3
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,560
I have to go to the den this evening.

4
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:35,840
Can you take Fon home for me?

5
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:39,240
I'll end this as soon as possible.

6
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:44,440
Where do you sell?
You ran out in less than a week.

7
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:45,480
Phetchaburi.

8
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:47,000
That's Oab's territory.

9
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:51,480
Where the hell is the gambling den?

10
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:57,520
I'll buy whatever you have.

11
00:01:57,600 --> 00:02:00,640
But you have to take me
to the person you get it from. Deal?

12
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:03,360
How much do you want this time?

13
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:08,759
Same as before.
But I've got a new seller. You interested?

14
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:12,480
He said he doesn't want anyone
to know he sells drugs.

15
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:14,400
So he wants to meet privately.

16
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:28,480
How about this? This time,

17
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:30,920
I'll buy whatever you have.

18
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:35,480
But you have to take me
to the person you get it from. Deal?

19
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,280
No.

20
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:45,120
I don't know you. I can't take you there.

21
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:50,080
Just get it from me for now.
We'll talk later.

22
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:55,920
Am I gonna get a commission out of this?
A bundle or two would be nice.

23
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:20,080
First time buying and you need that much?
You sure you can sell it?

24
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:24,400
Of course. I've got tons of customers.
There's barely any supply around there.

25
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:40,400
Take this much for now.
Come back when you're out.

26
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:54,320
I'm out of here.

27
00:04:21,959 --> 00:04:23,040
Go!

28
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:25,920
Hey!

29
00:04:58,280 --> 00:04:59,120
Damn.

30
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:04,640
Wasn't Oab at the gambling den?
Why is he back so soon?

31
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:07,480
Business has been up lately.

32
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:10,200
We'll probably have to go
to the den more often,

33
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:11,720
so the cash won't sit there too long.

34
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:13,240
Sounds good.

35
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:14,600
Here.

36
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:17,080
Same as usual?

37
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:18,680
Same as usual.

38
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:20,840
Take it to the foundations and hospitals.

39
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:22,760
You're gonna keep doing this forever?

40
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:24,600
Yeah.

41
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:32,960
You make a hundred, keep fifty.
You'll never get rich like this.

42
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:37,680
I've already got enough
to live comfortably. What more do I need?

43
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:43,320
We've taken a lot from people.
We should give some back.

44
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:47,720
The hospitals can use it
to buy equipment to treat people.

45
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:51,360
And kids who grew up
without a home like we did

46
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:53,320
can have a better future.

47
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:56,840
You're such a saint.

48
00:05:57,640 --> 00:06:00,200
Hey, take it to them tonight, okay?

49
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:07,040
Careful. Keep doing good deeds
and you'll die with no friends.

50
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:09,600
You'll get the good karma too.

51
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:11,800
Bless you, man.

52
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:13,320
I'm out.

53
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:23,840
- Where have you been?
- I went out to get some food.

54
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:46,440
Dom.

55
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:48,520
Yes?

56
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,480
You're not gonna eat?

57
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:02,120
I'm not hungry yet.

58
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:07,200
Did you ask Fon's father
about that matchbox yet?

59
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:10,280
Not yet.

60
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:12,120
Why didn't you ask?

61
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:16,120
Well, I'm not that close with her father.

62
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:17,960
But I asked someone else.

63
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:21,600
It's a matchbox
from Boss Koh's hotel in Khon Kaen.

64
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:24,120
Boss Koh is an influential figure.

65
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:26,600
He even has a group of hitmen.

66
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:57,840
You thought I'd pocket the money,
so you waited for me?

67
00:07:57,920 --> 00:07:59,400
Come on. Go to Khon Kaen with me.

68
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:01,680
I'm visiting someone I know.

69
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:04,600
- Didn't you just get back?
- Get the stuff ready too.

70
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:15,000
Damn it.
That bastard turned out to be a cop.

71
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:18,760
How am I supposed to face him
the next time I go get more stuff?

72
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:36,880
You know the cop you brought to us?

73
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:38,799
No, Boss. I don't.

74
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:44,360
You almost got me in trouble.

75
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:53,800
You won't make that mistake again.

76
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,080
Dom.

77
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:14,080
Where's Oab?

78
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:20,240
- He's not coming.
- Won't he get suspicious if you're gone?

79
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:24,640
He went out of town
and told me to look after you.

80
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:43,440
What's wrong? Why do you look like that?

81
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:55,240
I feel like I'm not doing enough for you.

82
00:09:58,240 --> 00:09:59,400
Don't be silly, Dom.

83
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:04,360
What you're doing is more than enough.

84
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:10,600
I just want this to end soon.

85
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:17,200
I know.

86
00:10:24,680 --> 00:10:26,920
How many days is he going to be gone?

87
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:29,560
He didn't say.

88
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:32,440
Did he say why he went?

89
00:10:33,760 --> 00:10:35,920
He went with Pong.
He didn't tell me anything else.

90
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:40,120
Could he be bringing drugs in
from the border?

91
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:44,800
No. At least so far,
I haven't seen him involved with drugs.

92
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:49,640
Then why don't you tell the chief?
He can put an end to this.

93
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:53,080
I already told him.
Right when I first joined.

94
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:57,960
Sir, there's no sign of drugs at all.

95
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:03,800
He even seems like a good person.

96
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:08,920
Sir, if you really want to arrest him,

97
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:11,800
isn't the gambling den enough?

98
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:16,600
Our people never found a gambling den,
just an empty building.

99
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:21,120
The locals won't say a word.
We know it's there, but no one's seen it.

100
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:24,320
I've never been to the den either.

101
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:26,880
He probably doesn't trust me.

102
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:28,880
How do you know there are no drugs?

103
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:32,200
I searched the entire boxing camp.
There really aren't any.

104
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:37,200
Then can't you make it look
like there are?

105
00:11:39,160 --> 00:11:40,400
But, Sir…

106
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:42,960
Everyone looks after their own future.

107
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:45,680
He gets his, and we lose ours.

108
00:11:55,520 --> 00:11:58,520
Dom, what did the chief say?

109
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:05,640
Dom, what did he say?

110
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:09,000
He didn't say anything.

111
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:14,040
Does he want you to keep going?

112
00:12:20,960 --> 00:12:24,280
But Champ did say
that since they sent people in,

113
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:26,640
you're the only one who's lasted this long

114
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:28,720
and gotten this close to Oab.

115
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:07,360
It looks the same.

116
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:10,600
The color's different.

117
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,080
What?

118
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:16,560
Go ask the staff for me.

119
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:19,480
I want one like this, but in gold.

120
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:28,920
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

121
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:32,000
I've had a box like this before,
but it was gold.

122
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:34,360
I don't see any on the table.
Do you have any left?

123
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:37,520
Oh, we don't have any left.
The gold ones are VIP-only.

124
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:39,440
Boss Koh keeps them to give out himself.

125
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:44,080
- Okay. Thank you.
- You're welcome.

126
00:13:47,440 --> 00:13:48,720
Come outside and talk to me.

127
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:54,560
You told me to bring the stuff
because you're going after Koh?

128
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:55,560
Yeah.

129
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:57,480
He's Peng's close friend.

130
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:59,720
He sent people to shoot me.

131
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:01,320
Are you sure about this?

132
00:14:02,160 --> 00:14:04,520
Why? Are you scared?

133
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:07,800
I'm more worried
Peng will send everyone after you.

134
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:10,040
Hey, if you guys
keep doing good work like this,

135
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:13,760
I'll take care of anything that comes up.
Got it?

136
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:15,920
- Yes, Boss.
- Good.

137
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:17,840
Listen carefully.

138
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:21,400
They need to know
that if they can't kill me,

139
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:23,920
they'll die.

140
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:33,240
How long have you been here?

141
00:14:33,320 --> 00:14:34,280
A little while.

142
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:38,680
Hey, if you ever need anything,

143
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:41,560
just give this matchbox to my staff.

144
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:45,480
- They'll take care of you.
- Got it. Thank you.

145
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:00,960
- I'll pick you up here this evening.
- Yeah.

146
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:06,960
It's nice having a husband
pick you up and drop you off.

147
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:14,800
I'll go now.

148
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:11,680
Where did he go?
He used to hang around here.

149
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:23,920
Excuse me. Have you seen a guy this tall
with a bob haircut?

150
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:28,880
Hurry, go check!
They said Chat has taken Pear hostage.

151
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:30,120
This way.

152
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:37,920
Get away!

153
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:40,000
- Don't come any closer!
- Hey, Chat.

154
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:42,720
Chat, calm down.

155
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:43,640
Go away!

156
00:16:43,720 --> 00:16:46,800
Chat, whatever you want, just say it.
Don't do anything to her.

157
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:49,080
I asked for it already.
She wouldn't give it to me.

158
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:50,240
- Hey, go get the police.
- Calm down.

159
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:51,800
Want me to get your mom for you?

160
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:53,320
- I'll go get her.
- Okay.

161
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,360
Let me through.

162
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:58,360
Hey.

163
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:02,160
What are you doing? Don't come any closer.

164
00:17:03,640 --> 00:17:06,200
Here, I'll give you this. You want it?

165
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:09,240
I don't want it.
You're trying to kill me, right?

166
00:17:09,319 --> 00:17:10,680
Why would I kill you?

167
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:14,040
- I don't believe you.
- I'll leave it here.

168
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:34,360
Go ahead.

169
00:17:53,880 --> 00:17:55,120
Ah! Let me go!

170
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:58,160
Hey! Let me go!

171
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:01,120
Ugh!

172
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:14,440
- Thank you.
- No problem.

173
00:18:15,080 --> 00:18:17,000
Thanks for walking me back to my shop.

174
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:19,600
I should get back to what I was doing.

175
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:20,760
Wait.

176
00:18:21,480 --> 00:18:25,120
Come sit inside first.
Let me treat you to some dessert.

177
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:27,680
It's my way of thanking you
for helping me earlier.

178
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:31,640
You don't have to.
I'm just glad you're not hurt.

179
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:37,520
At least let me clean your wound, okay?

180
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:49,840
- All done.
- Thanks.

181
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:53,760
Hold on. I'll go get some dessert for you.
Wait here.

182
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:09,240
Here you go.

183
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:14,360
You can eat dessert from my shop
for free for the rest of your life.

184
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:17,480
Thank you.

185
00:19:17,560 --> 00:19:18,640
You're welcome.

186
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:21,800
Honey, are you okay?

187
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:24,080
I was passing through the market
and heard what happened.

188
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:26,240
Are you hurt?

189
00:19:26,320 --> 00:19:28,120
He helped me, so I'm fine.

190
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:31,480
Dom, this is Liang, my husband.

191
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:36,920
Dom.

192
00:19:58,680 --> 00:19:59,640
It really is delicious.

193
00:20:00,640 --> 00:20:02,320
See? I told you it was good.

194
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:04,560
If Liang wasn't hooked on my desserts,

195
00:20:04,640 --> 00:20:06,920
he wouldn't come back
to see his wife every week.

196
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:10,800
He's always busy with work.
He only gets to come home once a week.

197
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:12,360
I miss him so much.

198
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:17,520
So how do you two know each other?

199
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:24,080
I work for the Department of Highways too,
like his boss.

200
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:30,440
Yeah. We've only met once or twice, right?

201
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:31,600
Yeah.

202
00:20:33,400 --> 00:20:34,640
I'd like to buy some dessert.

203
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:35,600
Coming.

204
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:46,720
- Did Oab send you here?
- No.

205
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:49,160
Then how did you know Pear is my wife?

206
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:52,160
I just found out.

207
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:56,320
I'm telling you the truth. I'm not lying.

208
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:06,280
Keep my wife a secret.

209
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:17,000
I'm asking you.

210
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:27,400
Is she your mistress?

211
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:32,080
She's the only one I have.

212
00:21:36,440 --> 00:21:39,640
She doesn't know what you do, does she?

213
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:47,760
I don't want her involved in my work.

214
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:50,720
It's better if she never knows.

215
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:55,600
People like us
shouldn't have someone we love.

216
00:21:56,960 --> 00:21:58,200
But if we do,

217
00:21:58,800 --> 00:22:01,240
shouldn't we protect them
more than ourselves?

218
00:22:11,720 --> 00:22:15,760
Hey, talking about work?
You two got carried away.

219
00:22:19,240 --> 00:22:20,560
Then I should get going.

220
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:25,120
I'll come by for dessert again sometime.

221
00:22:25,840 --> 00:22:26,880
Sure.

222
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:30,960
If I want to get to the parking lot,
which way do I go?

223
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:35,880
Honey, can you walk him
to the parking lot?

224
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:37,960
Sure.

225
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:45,280
I'll give you five minutes.

226
00:22:48,800 --> 00:22:51,040
Pong talked to you before
about joining Oab, right?

227
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:54,160
But you turned it down.
I want to know what you wanted.

228
00:22:56,280 --> 00:23:00,040
What I want is
something Oab can't give me.

229
00:23:01,240 --> 00:23:02,800
What can't he give you?

230
00:23:04,400 --> 00:23:05,480
Drugs.

231
00:23:08,200 --> 00:23:10,960
He has never gotten involved with drugs.

232
00:23:12,200 --> 00:23:13,160
Can he give me that?

233
00:23:16,600 --> 00:23:19,880
Times change. Things change too, Bro.

234
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:23,280
I'll talk to him if you're interested.

235
00:23:25,920 --> 00:23:28,160
Next week, I'll come back here

236
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:30,400
with an answer.

237
00:23:34,520 --> 00:23:37,400
SUPHAPHON SHOP

238
00:23:53,280 --> 00:23:56,000
Dom, want to go out for dinner tonight?

239
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:58,320
Let's eat at home.

240
00:24:00,200 --> 00:24:02,680
Can I stay over tonight?

241
00:24:03,960 --> 00:24:05,040
Okay.

242
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:12,160
- What happened to your arm?
- Boxing practice.

243
00:25:39,120 --> 00:25:41,760
I think I found a way to get Oab arrested.

244
00:25:45,040 --> 00:25:46,680
Why? What did you find?

245
00:25:49,440 --> 00:25:52,080
I didn't find anything. But I'm about to.

246
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:02,680
Dom, whatever you do, be careful.

247
00:26:03,680 --> 00:26:05,920
Don't frame him for something
he didn't do.

248
00:26:07,560 --> 00:26:09,080
Because in the end,

249
00:26:09,160 --> 00:26:11,920
if they find out it isn't true,

250
00:26:13,480 --> 00:26:14,640
he'll get away.

251
00:26:15,320 --> 00:26:18,720
And then you'll be the one in trouble.

252
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:24,000
I'm not framing him.

253
00:26:27,800 --> 00:26:31,440
But I think there's someone
who can make him agree to sell drugs.

254
00:26:48,040 --> 00:26:49,440
A hitman gang,

255
00:26:50,200 --> 00:26:53,440
drug dealers, running illegal brothels.

256
00:26:54,760 --> 00:26:56,240
They're just a waste of space.

257
00:27:01,080 --> 00:27:03,040
And they know Fon now.

258
00:27:04,360 --> 00:27:06,560
If I don't deal with them,
she won't be safe.

259
00:27:23,360 --> 00:27:25,280
We're closed. Go eat somewhere else. Hey!

260
00:27:27,680 --> 00:27:28,720
Ugh!

261
00:27:32,880 --> 00:27:34,040
You bastard!

262
00:28:37,240 --> 00:28:38,400
Goodbye, Sir.

263
00:28:41,320 --> 00:28:42,280
See you again.

264
00:28:44,360 --> 00:28:46,560
Boss, Boss Koh's been taken out.

265
00:28:48,120 --> 00:28:50,560
- Where?
- At a rice porridge shop downtown.

266
00:28:50,640 --> 00:28:54,240
Send someone to find out where Oab is.
I think he did it.

267
00:29:10,080 --> 00:29:11,360
We can't find him anywhere, Boss.

268
00:29:12,840 --> 00:29:14,520
He's nowhere?

269
00:29:16,640 --> 00:29:18,320
Did he really do it himself?

270
00:29:27,320 --> 00:29:30,480
After what you did,
you need to be more careful.

271
00:29:32,080 --> 00:29:35,960
I know. I've declared war on Peng.

272
00:29:43,960 --> 00:29:44,800
Hey, Pong.

273
00:29:48,360 --> 00:29:50,360
You can still walk away if you want.

274
00:29:52,040 --> 00:29:53,520
I'm here because of you.

275
00:29:55,720 --> 00:29:58,160
And I know no one worries about you
more than I do.

276
00:30:01,480 --> 00:30:03,400
We've been through a lot together.

277
00:30:05,960 --> 00:30:08,600
Even knowing you might die with me?

278
00:30:09,920 --> 00:30:13,840
You and I
are getting out of this together.

279
00:30:34,880 --> 00:30:36,640
I don't want to wake up.

280
00:30:40,240 --> 00:30:44,520
Go take a shower first.
I'll prepare breakfast for you.

281
00:30:55,240 --> 00:30:56,680
Go take a shower, okay?

282
00:31:55,560 --> 00:31:56,400
Fon.

283
00:31:58,160 --> 00:32:00,760
Come eat. Oab should be back today.

284
00:32:00,840 --> 00:32:03,040
After I drop you off, I need to

285
00:32:03,120 --> 00:32:05,720
hurry back and help Dum and Haw
set up the bar.

286
00:32:06,600 --> 00:32:08,840
So you won't be staying with me tonight?

287
00:32:11,720 --> 00:32:13,200
Will you miss me?

288
00:32:17,880 --> 00:32:21,400
Of course I will. I don't want you to go.

289
00:32:32,400 --> 00:32:33,880
Just hang in there, okay?

290
00:32:37,640 --> 00:32:40,680
Come on. Let's eat.

291
00:32:45,600 --> 00:32:47,080
Everything looks so good.

292
00:32:51,200 --> 00:32:52,720
I'll go take a shower first.

293
00:33:02,040 --> 00:33:04,600
Hey, did you hear about Boss Koh?
He got shot last night.

294
00:33:04,680 --> 00:33:06,760
Of course. It's all over the news.

295
00:33:15,480 --> 00:33:17,360
KHON KAEN CRIME BOSS SHOT DEAD
IN BRUTAL ATTACK AT RICE PORRIDGE SHOP

296
00:33:19,120 --> 00:33:20,680
<i>Then who were they?</i>

297
00:33:20,760 --> 00:33:22,400
<i>I'm not sure.</i>

298
00:33:22,480 --> 00:33:25,160
- He went out of town.
- Did he say why he went?

299
00:33:25,240 --> 00:33:26,440
He didn't tell me anything.

300
00:33:42,520 --> 00:33:43,600
Fon.

301
00:33:45,520 --> 00:33:46,680
What are you doing here?

302
00:33:47,280 --> 00:33:50,520
I was going to ask Dom.
Since I ran into you, I'll ask you.

303
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:54,080
About what?

304
00:33:54,880 --> 00:33:55,800
KHON KAEN CRIME BOSS SHOT DEAD

305
00:33:56,680 --> 00:33:59,920
You went out of town
to assassinate the Khon Kaen crime boss?

306
00:34:12,800 --> 00:34:14,360
You did, didn't you?

307
00:34:18,159 --> 00:34:20,960
Where are you going? Oab!

308
00:34:33,159 --> 00:34:34,719
- Haw.
- Yes, Bro?

309
00:34:34,800 --> 00:34:35,760
Is Dum in the back?

310
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:38,560
Yes. I don't know what he's doing though.

311
00:34:41,920 --> 00:34:44,560
Hey, what's wrong with you?

312
00:34:54,679 --> 00:34:56,400
She's not gonna choose you.

313
00:34:59,840 --> 00:35:02,440
He's handsome, rich, and influential.

314
00:35:02,520 --> 00:35:04,640
What is there
that a woman wouldn't like about him?

315
00:35:06,280 --> 00:35:08,120
Haw, do you know what you just said?

316
00:35:09,520 --> 00:35:10,560
Huh?

317
00:35:11,360 --> 00:35:12,840
You like your boss's woman.

318
00:35:19,640 --> 00:35:21,520
Haw, what the hell are you saying?

319
00:35:21,600 --> 00:35:23,440
If anyone hears you, I'm screwed.

320
00:35:25,640 --> 00:35:26,840
What are you smiling about?

321
00:35:27,520 --> 00:35:28,840
You didn't deny it.

322
00:35:29,640 --> 00:35:31,960
You're crazy. I don't like Fon.

323
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:35,040
Keep telling yourself that.

324
00:35:44,240 --> 00:35:46,800
- What?
- Dom.

325
00:35:48,440 --> 00:35:49,680
I've got eyes, you know.

326
00:35:50,680 --> 00:35:53,520
I saw the way you look at her.

327
00:35:55,320 --> 00:35:56,600
Even a fool could tell.

328
00:35:58,480 --> 00:36:00,880
And I believe if Oab saw it,

329
00:36:01,800 --> 00:36:03,360
he'd figure you out for sure.

330
00:36:06,040 --> 00:36:08,160
I share a room with you.

331
00:36:08,760 --> 00:36:10,480
Oab wasn't here yesterday,

332
00:36:11,760 --> 00:36:12,800
so where did you go?

333
00:36:14,560 --> 00:36:16,560
He told me to watch over Fon.

334
00:36:19,320 --> 00:36:20,880
But you came back in the same clothes.

335
00:36:23,440 --> 00:36:25,320
You had to sleep in a car.

336
00:36:25,840 --> 00:36:29,960
It was hot, and you didn't even shower.

337
00:36:33,600 --> 00:36:34,480
What the hell?

338
00:36:35,520 --> 00:36:37,960
But you smell
like someone who just took a shower.

339
00:36:39,520 --> 00:36:41,200
Let me guess…

340
00:36:41,280 --> 00:36:42,280
Don't guess.

341
00:36:44,040 --> 00:36:46,480
I used the guard's bathroom to shower.

342
00:36:46,560 --> 00:36:50,720
Who could stand being all sweaty
in the same clothes day and night?

343
00:36:52,720 --> 00:36:53,880
- Good.
- Yeah.

344
00:36:53,960 --> 00:36:54,800
Good.

345
00:36:55,600 --> 00:36:57,120
As long as there's nothing going on.

346
00:36:57,640 --> 00:36:59,280
I'm just worried about you.

347
00:37:00,440 --> 00:37:02,600
If it wasn't me who noticed this earlier,

348
00:37:03,480 --> 00:37:04,760
you'd be screwed.

349
00:37:06,320 --> 00:37:08,560
Whatever you're feeling,
keep it to yourself.

350
00:37:09,720 --> 00:37:11,200
I won't tell anyone.

351
00:37:12,600 --> 00:37:14,960
Consider it a secret between you and me.

352
00:37:15,640 --> 00:37:17,200
I'll take it to my grave.

353
00:37:41,200 --> 00:37:44,400
You had to bring me all the way here
just to answer a question?

354
00:37:58,200 --> 00:37:59,160
Let's take a walk.

355
00:38:02,040 --> 00:38:03,960
You're not going to answer
my question, right?

356
00:38:31,160 --> 00:38:34,400
Are you staying quiet
because you don't want to answer?

357
00:38:35,360 --> 00:38:36,320
I don't want to answer.

358
00:38:37,840 --> 00:38:39,080
But I have a question.

359
00:38:43,480 --> 00:38:46,920
Okay. If I answer your question,

360
00:38:47,640 --> 00:38:51,560
you have to answer mine too.
Whether or not you did it.

361
00:38:52,800 --> 00:38:53,680
Okay.

362
00:38:56,120 --> 00:38:57,360
Then ask.

363
00:38:59,640 --> 00:39:01,080
After me,

364
00:39:02,920 --> 00:39:04,520
have you dated anyone else?

365
00:39:09,640 --> 00:39:11,040
Why are you asking that?

366
00:39:12,240 --> 00:39:14,800
You've been avoiding me all this time.
You never answered

367
00:39:15,360 --> 00:39:16,920
whether you'd be with me.

368
00:39:19,360 --> 00:39:20,240
How about this?

369
00:39:21,800 --> 00:39:23,800
If you answer me,

370
00:39:23,880 --> 00:39:25,480
I'll answer your question.

371
00:39:31,600 --> 00:39:32,440
Okay.

372
00:39:34,000 --> 00:39:37,080
Well, I did date someone.

373
00:39:38,080 --> 00:39:40,640
- Are you still with him?
- One question.

374
00:39:41,240 --> 00:39:42,840
I answered yours.

375
00:39:43,440 --> 00:39:44,400
Now it's your turn.

376
00:40:03,480 --> 00:40:04,520
I didn't do it.

377
00:40:09,840 --> 00:40:11,680
But someone like Boss Koh

378
00:40:13,040 --> 00:40:14,280
deserved to die anyway.

379
00:40:17,800 --> 00:40:20,560
I think you chose
not to tell me the truth.

380
00:40:21,520 --> 00:40:23,240
You want to hear the truth?

381
00:40:32,280 --> 00:40:34,680
The truth will make you see me
differently.

382
00:40:36,000 --> 00:40:37,320
But at least,

383
00:40:38,000 --> 00:40:41,240
it'll show me
that you're being honest with me.

384
00:40:52,000 --> 00:40:53,560
If I didn't kill him today,

385
00:40:55,520 --> 00:40:57,520
he would've found a chance
to kill me anyway.

386
00:41:07,760 --> 00:41:09,160
That's not okay, is it?

387
00:41:14,480 --> 00:41:16,040
I understand.

388
00:41:18,480 --> 00:41:21,320
Once you're in too deep,
it's hard to get out.

389
00:41:24,520 --> 00:41:26,720
But that doesn't mean you can't get out.

390
00:41:31,120 --> 00:41:32,400
Just have to plan it carefully.

391
00:41:39,440 --> 00:41:40,520
Are you going to quit?

392
00:41:48,520 --> 00:41:50,680
You're really going to walk away
from this life?

393
00:41:52,920 --> 00:41:56,080
But it gives you money and power.

394
00:41:57,480 --> 00:41:59,680
Can you really leave all that behind?

395
00:42:02,040 --> 00:42:03,840
Ever since I found you again,

396
00:42:05,600 --> 00:42:07,480
I've felt like I can.

397
00:42:30,640 --> 00:42:34,200
I got word that Oab and Pong
aren't in Bangkok, Boss.

398
00:42:36,240 --> 00:42:39,600
I knew it. It has to be Oab's doing.

399
00:42:40,760 --> 00:42:42,880
They must have figured out

400
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:45,600
who attacked them in Khon Kaen.

401
00:42:48,680 --> 00:42:50,280
He went after my people.

402
00:42:51,320 --> 00:42:52,800
I'll go after his.

403
00:42:55,800 --> 00:42:56,880
Come in.

404
00:43:04,040 --> 00:43:04,920
I'm here, Boss.

405
00:43:21,200 --> 00:43:22,480
Pong.

406
00:43:24,440 --> 00:43:26,800
Dum's in a hurry,
so he went to wait at the gambling den.

407
00:43:38,600 --> 00:43:41,760
- You're only selling one brand of liquor?
- It's better than nothing.

408
00:43:42,720 --> 00:43:43,720
Why?

409
00:43:44,800 --> 00:43:48,440
No one would sell us liquor
because everyone's afraid of Peng.

410
00:43:51,240 --> 00:43:53,360
But luckily, Dom managed to make a deal.

411
00:43:57,920 --> 00:43:59,040
Hey.

412
00:44:00,480 --> 00:44:04,280
If this bar does well,
I'll open another one for you.

413
00:44:10,080 --> 00:44:10,920
Go sit down, Fon.

414
00:44:17,200 --> 00:44:18,440
You must be happy.

415
00:44:20,160 --> 00:44:23,920
You won't find a boss better than him.
I guarantee it.

416
00:44:45,360 --> 00:44:49,480
Geez, there's so much dust.
Looks like we have to clean all of this.

417
00:44:51,920 --> 00:44:53,080
Pong.

418
00:44:53,680 --> 00:44:55,840
Go grab some food. We'll just eat here.

419
00:44:56,880 --> 00:44:58,160
Get enough for everyone.

420
00:44:58,760 --> 00:45:01,320
Take Haw with you to help.

421
00:45:01,880 --> 00:45:03,480
- Come on, Haw.
- Yes.

422
00:45:07,320 --> 00:45:08,800
I'll wash the dishes.

423
00:45:08,880 --> 00:45:09,720
Huh?

424
00:45:09,800 --> 00:45:11,320
So we have something to eat with.

425
00:45:11,400 --> 00:45:12,440
Let me help.

426
00:45:12,520 --> 00:45:16,800
Just wait here, Oab. I'll do it.

427
00:45:39,080 --> 00:45:39,960
Oab.

428
00:45:41,240 --> 00:45:43,000
Are you still interested in Liang?

429
00:45:45,040 --> 00:45:46,040
Peng's guy?

430
00:45:46,680 --> 00:45:47,520
Yes.

431
00:45:49,200 --> 00:45:50,880
Why would I be interested in him?

432
00:45:50,960 --> 00:45:53,720
I heard you used to be interested in him

433
00:45:53,800 --> 00:45:56,360
because you wanted
his info on Peng, right?

434
00:45:59,320 --> 00:46:00,240
What have you got?

435
00:46:03,320 --> 00:46:05,480
If we stay quiet, he'll walk all over us.

436
00:46:05,560 --> 00:46:06,520
I know.

437
00:46:06,600 --> 00:46:08,080
So are you going to take him out?

438
00:46:08,720 --> 00:46:11,120
Boss knows what he's doing.

439
00:46:12,840 --> 00:46:14,560
You guys just stay quiet for now.

440
00:46:28,040 --> 00:46:29,520
If you let this go,

441
00:46:30,120 --> 00:46:31,640
who's going to respect you?

442
00:46:32,840 --> 00:46:34,600
I know how to deal with him.

443
00:46:37,600 --> 00:46:41,080
An eye for an eye, a tooth for a tooth.

444
00:46:53,840 --> 00:46:55,520
Are you done with your work outside?

445
00:46:55,600 --> 00:46:58,760
Not yet.
But Pong already brought the food back.

446
00:47:07,960 --> 00:47:10,440
Dom, someone might see us.

447
00:47:18,800 --> 00:47:20,520
Can I stay here with you a little longer?

448
00:47:35,080 --> 00:47:36,680
Can I get some plates?

449
00:47:39,680 --> 00:47:42,040
Here. They're clean. Just dry them.

450
00:47:45,080 --> 00:47:46,320
Once you're done, leave.

451
00:48:22,480 --> 00:48:24,040
If you were me, what would you do?

452
00:48:25,240 --> 00:48:27,080
<i>Liang said that</i>

453
00:48:27,160 --> 00:48:30,120
if you let him sell drugs
in your territory,

454
00:48:30,800 --> 00:48:32,360
he'd agree to negotiate.

455
00:48:57,600 --> 00:49:00,760
Do I really have to do something
I've opposed my whole life?

456
00:49:24,280 --> 00:49:26,080
<i>If I didn't kill him today,</i>

457
00:49:27,480 --> 00:49:29,600
<i>he would've found a chance</i>
<i>to kill me anyway.</i>

458
00:49:48,720 --> 00:49:51,720
Dad, are you still awake?

459
00:49:55,160 --> 00:49:58,440
I wanted to ask about the case
that was just in the newspaper.

460
00:49:58,520 --> 00:50:01,480
The hotel owner who was shot
in front of the rice porridge shop.

461
00:50:02,840 --> 00:50:04,880
Do the police know who did it?

462
00:50:12,200 --> 00:50:13,320
Come on.

463
00:50:18,280 --> 00:50:19,400
Hit me.

464
00:50:22,280 --> 00:50:24,160
Whoa. Ow!

465
00:50:28,040 --> 00:50:30,760
Ouch! Dom!

466
00:50:33,920 --> 00:50:37,560
Taking out your frustration
from yesterday? Go on, take a break.

467
00:50:37,640 --> 00:50:38,640
Go.

468
00:50:38,720 --> 00:50:40,520
NO GAMBLING

469
00:50:49,040 --> 00:50:50,760
You're really fired up today.

470
00:50:50,840 --> 00:50:54,120
Throwing punches nonstop
like some martial arts master.

471
00:50:55,120 --> 00:50:56,440
Are you trying to vent?

472
00:51:02,760 --> 00:51:04,160
I'm getting some water.

473
00:51:06,960 --> 00:51:08,080
Where are you going?

474
00:51:08,680 --> 00:51:11,200
Geez! You're not even going to rest?

475
00:51:15,640 --> 00:51:16,720
Two!

476
00:51:19,000 --> 00:51:20,120
Dom.

477
00:51:23,000 --> 00:51:24,040
Come with me for a bit.

478
00:51:44,280 --> 00:51:46,120
I wanted you to see the place
where I grew up.

479
00:51:48,960 --> 00:51:51,120
A lot of kids end up here

480
00:51:52,320 --> 00:51:54,560
because they've been affected by drugs.

481
00:51:58,240 --> 00:52:02,080
If it weren't for this place, I don't know
what kind of person I would have become.

482
00:52:02,160 --> 00:52:05,640
You brought me here
because I talked to you about Liang

483
00:52:05,720 --> 00:52:07,840
wanting to sell drugs
in your territory, right?

484
00:52:08,440 --> 00:52:09,480
Yeah.

485
00:52:12,760 --> 00:52:15,080
Do you know why I never sell drugs?

486
00:52:15,800 --> 00:52:20,400
Even though I run a gambling den,
own a bar, and do illegal things.

487
00:52:25,960 --> 00:52:29,920
My dad was addicted to drugs
and beat my mom every day.

488
00:52:33,360 --> 00:52:36,280
I don't want any kid
to go through what I did.

489
00:52:41,360 --> 00:52:43,560
So you're not going to agree
to Liang's deal?

490
00:52:51,280 --> 00:52:52,560
But if you do,

491
00:52:53,520 --> 00:52:55,640
you can get revenge
for your younger brother.

492
00:53:12,800 --> 00:53:15,040
- Haw.
- Yes, Bro.

493
00:53:15,880 --> 00:53:18,680
- Have you seen Oab?
- I saw him this morning.

494
00:53:20,040 --> 00:53:23,240
- Where did he go? Did he tell you?
- He took Dom somewhere.

495
00:53:31,280 --> 00:53:32,400
Go collect the money.

496
00:53:32,480 --> 00:53:35,960
He's owed us for months.
I've asked him three times. No payment.

497
00:53:36,640 --> 00:53:37,720
- Yes.
- Alright.

498
00:53:38,320 --> 00:53:39,480
Hey, Don.

499
00:53:42,960 --> 00:53:44,400
Wait for me a second.

500
00:54:07,040 --> 00:54:08,840
What are you and that kid planning?

501
00:54:09,520 --> 00:54:10,520
What are you talking about?

502
00:54:11,680 --> 00:54:14,640
You're planning something
and you don't want me to know.

503
00:54:20,160 --> 00:54:23,120
- What are you up to?
- I just took him to the foundation.

504
00:54:23,200 --> 00:54:24,320
You think I'd believe that?

505
00:54:25,440 --> 00:54:29,160
I'm not stupid, you know.
What are you two up to?

506
00:54:30,720 --> 00:54:33,440
I noticed you haven't slept
these past few days.

507
00:54:33,520 --> 00:54:35,680
So I had Dom drive me today. That's all.

508
00:54:36,280 --> 00:54:37,200
Are you sure?

509
00:54:49,640 --> 00:54:50,480
Is something wrong?

510
00:54:54,000 --> 00:54:55,240
What does it say?

511
00:54:56,640 --> 00:54:58,400
A life for a life.

512
00:55:04,880 --> 00:55:08,160
A LIFE FOR A LIFE

513
00:55:15,480 --> 00:55:20,200
Two grilled pork skewers
with sticky rice, please. How much is it?

514
00:56:06,880 --> 00:56:08,120
Can't you drive any faster?

515
00:56:08,200 --> 00:56:09,800
That car cut in front of me.

516
00:56:42,800 --> 00:56:44,400
Hey!

517
00:56:47,480 --> 00:56:48,760
Shit.

518
00:56:50,800 --> 00:56:53,920
- Fon!
- Fon!

519
00:56:56,160 --> 00:56:59,840
- Fon!
- Fon, can you hear me? Fon!

520
00:57:03,280 --> 00:57:04,840
She still has a pulse.

521
00:57:06,320 --> 00:57:08,680
Go to Crime Suppression. Get an ambulance.

522
00:57:09,440 --> 00:57:10,400
Now!

523
00:57:11,760 --> 00:57:12,680
Fon.

524
00:57:26,800 --> 00:57:28,400
Peng must be behind this.

525
00:57:28,480 --> 00:57:29,760
Enough, Dom.

526
00:57:29,840 --> 00:57:31,640
Can we stop this?

527
00:57:31,720 --> 00:57:34,640
The cycle of revenge ends
when you choose not to take revenge.

528
00:57:34,720 --> 00:57:38,040
Whatever you can let go of, let it go now.

529
00:57:38,120 --> 00:57:42,400
Don't chase after things
beyond your reach.

530
00:57:42,480 --> 00:57:43,920
It may be better to step back now

531
00:57:44,560 --> 00:57:48,160
than keep chasing
until you can't turn back.

532
00:57:49,680 --> 00:57:51,120
If I give up now,

533
00:57:52,280 --> 00:57:54,320
I'll never be good enough for Fon.

534
00:57:54,400 --> 00:57:57,280
Just tell me who did it

535
00:57:57,920 --> 00:57:58,880
and where they are.

536
00:58:43,720 --> 00:58:45,600
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
